The repo root directory is not the project directory. When you want to run a julia command (e.g. `julia --project=.`) remember that the project directory is usually ./Planar or ./PlanarDev or ./PlanarOptim depending on which part of the project we are working on (usually PlanarDev, so the command would be `julia --project=./PlanarDev`). Most subdirectories of repo root are project directories (the ones with a Project.toml file). NEVER use `julia --project=.`, there is no Project.toml in the root d...